  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Activated Expedition Map to search for a land (goes to hand, can't play until next turn) instead of casting Planar Atlas, which costs the same 2 mana but stays on the battlefield as a permanent mana source AND filters the top 4 cards for a land. With only Urza's Tower as a land and needing to develop mana, the permanent ramp from Planar Atlas is more valuable than just tutoring a land to hand.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Expedition Map ({2}, tap, sacrifice) to search for a land card to put in hand.",
      "better_line": "Cast Planar Atlas for {2} to get a permanent mana source and filter top 4 for a land, preserving Expedition Map for later when there's spare mana.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 32,
      "player": "Haiku Perfect",
      "decision_index": 19,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Playing Awakener Druid with only one Forest on the battlefield risks losing the only green mana source if either the Druid or the animated Forest is removed. The opponent has blue mana and 5 cards in hand, potentially including removal like Waterknot.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Awakener Druid, animating the only Forest into a 4/5 creature",
      "better_line": "Cast Planar Atlas to develop mana, search for Urza's Mine (working toward Tron), and preserve the Forest as a safe mana source. Could then cast bigger threats next turn with more mana available.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 54,
      "player": "Haiku Perfect",
      "decision_index": 30,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Used Waterknot when Sailor of Means would develop the board and create a Treasure token to accelerate toward Courser of Kruphix (turn 5) and Rampaging Baloths (turn 6). The opponent's threats are all tapped/sick this turn, so there's no immediate need for removal. Master's Rebuke in hand could also deal with the 4/5 Treefolk later if needed.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Waterknot (presumably targeting the 4/5 Forest Treefolk or Awakener Druid) using all available mana",
      "better_line": "Play Island, cast Sailor of Means (1/4 blocker + Treasure token), accelerating toward Courser of Kruphix next turn and Rampaging Baloths soon after. Save Waterknot or Master's Rebuke for later if the Treefolk becomes problematic.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 69,
      "player": "G31FL Stats",
      "decision_index": 36,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Urza's Factory (enters tapped) instead of Forest costs 1 mana this turn. Forest would enter untapped, providing 4 mana total and enabling casting Thaumaturge's Familiar (3) + Universal Solvent (1) in the same turn. Forest also provides green mana needed for future spells. Urza's Factory doesn't complete Tron (missing Power-Plant) and its 7-mana activation is very expensive.",
      "action_taken": "Played Urza's Factory (enters tapped), leaving only 3 mana available this turn",
      "better_line": "Play Forest (enters untapped) for 4 mana this turn, enabling more efficient sequencing like Thaumaturge's Familiar + Universal Solvent. Save Urza's Factory for a turn where the tempo loss of a tapped land matters less.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 91,
      "player": "Haiku Perfect",
      "decision_index": 45,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed priority in postcombat main with 2 untapped mana and Universal Solvent (costs {1}) available to cast. Universal Solvent is a pure-upside deployment — getting it on the battlefield early gives future access to its {7},{T},sacrifice removal ability at no cost. Walking Ballista as X=1 (1/1) was also castable with the remaining mana.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, ending the turn with 2 mana unused and castable spells in hand.",
      "better_line": "Cast Universal Solvent for {1} to deploy it for future use. Could also consider Walking Ballista for X=1 with the remaining mana, or save 1 mana. At minimum, Universal Solvent should have been played.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 111,
      "player": "Haiku Perfect",
      "decision_index": 60,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Walking Ballista as a 2/2 (X=2, 4 mana) instead of Golem Artisan (3/3 for 5 mana). With Tron completing next turn (Urza's Power Plant in hand), Golem Artisan's repeatable pump and keyword-granting abilities would be extremely powerful with 10+ mana available. Golem Artisan is both a bigger body now and has far more upside with the massive mana coming online.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Walking Ballista for X=2 as a 2/2, leaving 1 mana unused",
      "better_line": "Cast Golem Artisan (3/3 for 5 mana) to maximize board presence and set up its powerful activated abilities with Tron mana coming next turn",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 133,
      "player": "Haiku Perfect",
      "decision_index": 71,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Activated Walking Ballista to ping for 1 damage (likely to face or a 4-toughness creature that won't die), shrinking the 4/4 Ballista to 3/3, instead of deploying Universal Solvent which has significant future utility as a permanent destruction threat, especially with Urza Tron lands available.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Walking Ballista to remove a +1/+1 counter and deal 1 damage",
      "better_line": "Cast Universal Solvent for {1} to deploy a threat that can later destroy any permanent for {7}, preserving Walking Ballista's 4/4 body for combat",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 142,
      "player": "Haiku Perfect",
      "decision_index": 76,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Removed a +1/+1 counter from Walking Ballista (reducing it from 4/4 to 3/3) just to deal 1 damage to the opponent's face at 20 life. The 1 point of face damage is nearly meaningless while the counter has significant value keeping Ballista larger for combat. The Ballista is sick and can't attack this turn anyway, but the counter should be preserved for future use - either to kill an actual threat, finish off a damaged creature, or maintain board presence as a larger body.",
      "action_taken": "Pinged opponent's face for 1 damage with Walking Ballista, reducing it from 4/4 to 3/3.",
      "better_line": "Hold the counter on Walking Ballista to maintain it as a 4/4 for future combat or save the ping for a more impactful target later.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 142,
      "player": "Haiku Perfect",
      "decision_index": 76,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Shrinking Walking Ballista from 4/4 to 3/3 to deal 1 damage to opponent's face is poor value. The opponent is at 20 life, so 1 ping is negligible, while the Ballista loses significant combat presence. No opponent creature dies to just 1 damage, so there's no efficient removal available either. The Ballista should be preserved at full size to attack next turn.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Walking Ballista to ping opponent's face for 1, reducing it from 4/4 to 3/3.",
      "better_line": "Don't activate Walking Ballista at all. Keep it at 4/4 to maximize its combat threat next turn when summoning sickness wears off. Save counter removal for when it can finish off a creature or deal lethal damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 143,
      "player": "Haiku Perfect",
      "decision_index": 78,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Removed the last +1/+1 counter from Walking Ballista to deal 1 damage to the opponent at 20 life, killing the Ballista. With Urza's Tron assembled, the Ballista could have been grown with its {4} activated ability in future turns, making it a significant threat. All three pings going to face at 20 life is low-value; the first two pings were already committed but saving the last counter would have kept the Ballista alive.",
      "action_taken": "Removed the third and final +1/+1 counter from Walking Ballista to deal 1 damage to opponent's face (total 3 damage to a 20-life opponent), killing the Ballista.",
      "better_line": "Decline to activate the third time, keeping Walking Ballista as a 1/1. With Tron online generating 7+ mana, Ballista could be grown with its {4} ability to add counters, becoming a much larger threat over time. A 1/1 body also blocks, carries equipment, and provides future flexibility.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 145,
      "player": "Haiku Perfect",
      "decision_index": 81,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Walking Ballista had 2 +1/+1 counters and Tron was assembled (Urza's Mine + Power Plant + Tower), generating 7+ mana. Instead of keeping Ballista alive and using the {4} ability to grow it into a serious threat, the player is removing all counters to deal just 2 damage to an opponent at 20 life, killing the Ballista for negligible impact.",
      "action_taken": "Removed +1/+1 counters from Walking Ballista to deal 2 damage to opponent at 20 life, killing the Ballista",
      "better_line": "Keep Walking Ballista alive with its counters. With Tron assembled, use {4} to add +1/+1 counters each turn, growing it into a major threat. A 2/2 that can grow with excess mana is far more valuable than 2 damage to a 20-life opponent.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 147,
      "player": "Haiku Perfect",
      "decision_index": 84,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Haiku Perfect activated Urza's Factory during combat to create a 2/2 token, which uses up all the Tron mana (7 generic + tap Factory). This prevents casting Ulvenwald Hydra in the postcombat main phase. With the Forest in hand played post-combat, they would have had exactly enough mana (2 Forests for GG + Tron lands for 4 colorless) to cast the 6-mana Ulvenwald Hydra, which would enter as approximately a 7/7 with reach, and tutor a land (potentially becoming 8/8). A 7/7+ reach that tutors a land is vastly superior to a 2/2 token.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Urza's Factory during combat to create a 2/2 Assembly-Worker token, tapping all Tron lands.",
      "better_line": "Pass during combat, then in postcombat main phase play Forest from hand, then cast Ulvenwald Hydra (4GG) using both Forests and Tron lands. Hydra enters as ~7/7 reach and tutors another land to the battlefield.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 197,
      "player": "Haiku Perfect",
      "decision_index": 106,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Spent 8 mana (7 + tap Factory) during combat to create a 2/2 Assembly-Worker token, when the mana could have been used postcombat to cast Golem Artisan (5 mana, 3/3 with pump abilities for artifact creatures) which is strictly better. The 2/2 token can't even attack this turn since it was just created during combat.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Urza's Factory to create a 2/2 token during combat, using essentially all available mana",
